**objectstack-ai/objectui#12113** (p3; director ruling `6105451919`, letter A1, maintainer 「同意」; claim `6109802426`; branch `claude/issue-12113-retire-studio-home`). `StudioHomePage` retires, and the Studio app's root resolves to its own first navigation item.

- **The one file in your territory:** `apps/console/src/__tests__/AppContent.systemHubRoutes.test.tsx`, which C9 part 1 (PR objectui#12089, `0df67f2`) edited. Only its references to `StudioHomePage` are deleted or re-pointed.
- **The rest of the surface:**
  - app-shell's `AppContent.tsx` (the app index route's last fallback, and `resolveLandingRoute` learning `component` items);
  - `UnifiedSidebar.tsx` (the Studio-only Home entry);
  - `StudioHomePage.tsx` and its export and tests, all deleted;
  - its readers `useRecentItemLabel.ts`, `ContextSelectors.tsx` and `AppNoAccessEmptyState.tsx`, and the note in `appServesNoNavigation.ts`;
  - the `engine.home.*` strings only that page reads;
  - the other tests that name the page, docs and one changeset.
- **What does not change:** ⛔ the Setup catalog pages, `ResourceListPage`, `ResourceEditPage`, `PermissionMatrixEditor`, `AssignedUsersSection`, `PositionHoldersSection`, `catalog-activation.ts`, `catalog-scope.ts`, console `apps/console/src/AppContent.tsx`, and every other region your C9 stage edited.
- **Serial:** no open objectui PR touches `metadata-admin/` or these files at this stamp. If C9 part 2 opens on the same test file first, this card merges `main` and keeps both.

